.TH DIPIBIM 1 "2026-10-19" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipibim \- convert between XML and its BiM binary encoding through an XML Schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipibim
.B \-f
.I xml
.B \-s
.I <schema>
[\fB\-i\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipibim
.B \-f
.I bim
.B \-s
.I <schema>
[\fB\-i\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipibim
converts between XML and its BiM binary encoding (ISO/IEC 15938-1:2002,
ISO/IEC 23001-1:2006 with Cor 1, Cor 2, Amd 1 and Amd 2). Schemas are loaded
from XSD files at runtime. \fB\-f\fR names the input format, the output is the
other one.
.PP
A schema is one file or any number of directories (\fB\-s\fR). A directory is
searched recursively for the schema declaring the namespace of the input root
element (\fB\-f xml\fR) or of SchemaURI[0] in the stream (\fB\-f bim\fR).
Imports and includes resolve in the directories and next to the schema file.
.PP
The profile selects the stream layout:
.TP
.B dvb-tva
DVB-TVA-init (ETSI TS 102 323 table 53), then [4-byte big-endian length][DVBBiMAccessUnit]
[string repository], the access unit as TS 102 323 tables 56/57 with the DVB codecs of
subclause 9.4.3. A TVAMain document is split into fragments (TS 102 822-3-2 table 7).
Documents that break the content rules of TS 102 323 clause 8 are refused.
.TP
.B tva
TVA-init and BiMAccessUnit of TS 102 822-3-2 subclause 4.4, Zlib strings, tvadateTime and tvadate codecs.
Needs zlib.
.TP
.B sdns
DVB-TVA-init and one ServiceDiscovery segment with DVBContextPath 0x0030 (TS 102 034 subclause 5.5), Zlib strings.
Needs zlib.
.TP
.B generic
DecoderInit and one access unit with one topmost element (ISO/IEC 23001-1).
.PP
No mapping table:
.B dipibim
does not touch xmltv ids or URIs, it is a wire-format conversion only.
No DVBSTP container, index structures or versioning (ETSI TS 102 822-3-2, subclauses 4.5/4.6) are
produced or expected; see
.BR dipibcg (1)
for that layer. The plain TVA XML of
.BR dipixmltv (1)
converts directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input\ \fI<path>\fR
Input path, \fB\-\fR for stdin. Default: stdin.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\ \fI<path>\fR
Output path, \fB\-\fR for stdout. Default: stdout.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format\ \fI<fmt>\fR
.IR xml | bim .
Names the input format; required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-schema\ \fI<path>\fR
Schema file, or directory searched for schemas by namespace. Repeatable. Required. One file is used as is,
of several the one declaring the namespace. The schemas listed after SchemaURI[0] in the DecoderInit of a
stream are found the same way, the chunks of those not found are skipped.
The encoders list the namespaces of the document that the main schema does not define as further schemas,
when a schema file for them is found.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fI<name>\fR
.IR dvb\-tva | tva | sdns | generic .
Default: \fBdvb\-tva\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-syntax \fI<name>\fR
.IR 23001\-1 | 15938\-1 .
Payload syntax of the generic profile. Default: \fB23001\-1\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-compat \fI<name>\fR[,\fI<name>\fR...]
Deviations of the MPEG-7 Systems conformance streams from the standard text, off by default:
.BR no\-schema\-mode " (no SchemaModeUpdate with several schemas),"
.BR time\-flags " (time points and durations as the reference software codes them),"
.BR attr\-local " (attributes ordered by local name),"
.BR fixed\-attr " (optional fixed attributes coded),"
.BR list\-string " (IDREFS, NMTOKENS and ENTITIES as strings),"
.B conformance
(all of these). The 169 single access unit streams of the suite decode with
.BR "\-\-profile generic \-\-syntax 15938\-1 \-\-compat conformance" .
.TP
.B \-\-len\-mode \fI<n>\fR
lengthCodingMode 0, 1 or 2. generic, default 0.
.TP
.B \-\-deferred
hasDeferredNodes. generic.
.TP
.B \-\-cast
hasTypeCasting. generic.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-locator
Optimized locator coding where the decoder renders the same text. dvb-tva.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-duration
Minute coding of durations where exact. dvb-tva.
.TP
.B \-\-dvb\-pubtime
PublishedTime coding of dateTime where representable. dvb-tva.
.TP
.B \-\-zbuf\-size \fI<bytes>\fR
Zlib BufferSize, 0 for 1000. tva and sdns.
.TP
.B \-\-zgather
Gather strings up to BufferSize per Zlib chunk. tva and sdns.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\ \fI<path>\fR
YAML configuration file. Keys are the long option names. Without this option,
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipibim.yaml
is read if it exists. Command line options override the file.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-strict
Configuration file issues are errors.
.TP
.B \-\-configtest
Check the configuration file, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
One line on stderr: fragment count and output size.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipibim.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dvbipitools/etc/dipibim.yaml
Example configuration file (Debian).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipibim \-f xml \-s schemas/ \-i guide.tva.xml \-o guide.bim
Encode a TVAMain document to its BiM binary form.
.TP
.B dipibim \-f bim \-s schemas/ \-i guide.bim \-o guide.tva.xml
Decode it back.
.TP
.B dipibim \-f xml \-s schemas/ \-\-profile sdns \-i sds.xml \-o sds.bim
Encode an SD&S segment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipixmltv (1),
.BR dipibcg (1)
.PP
